onna be  very sanitized they want to make sure  that no one criticizes them that no one  files a complaint so they're gonna  anything controversial they're gonna  take it out of the broadcast now you  could say that youtubers who don't care  about making money can still make the  kind of videos they want to make and  that is true however while there are  quality youtubers out there who take  YouTube as just a hobby and not a job  the fact is that if they are working on  YouTube and also have a full-time job  somewhere else they are most likely  gonna be making a lot less videos and  making videos a lot less frequently than  someone who is actually treating YouTube  as a full-time job so those YouTube  creators  do you want to make YouTube their job  and want to bring out regular frequent  content to their fans are in a big  dilemma now do they have to shift their  entire approach completely do they have  to start making completely different  videos in order to become  family-friendly or do they stick to what  they're doing even if they are risking  potentially not being able to make ends  meet and pay their bills the other big  problem is that this new flagging system  doesn't even work properly every single  video that we had flagged on our Channel  and we requested a review for because  you now have the option to request a  review was approved meaning they said  yes the system made a mistake this video  is fine for all advertisers so clearly  something is wrong here and while it is  definitely a good thing that you now  have the option to request a review  because a few weeks ago you didn't even  have that the problem is that each video  when they first come out your  subscribers receive a notification as  soon as the video comes out and then  they watch it so if your video is  falsely flagged as unsuitable for all  advertisers as soon as it comes out for  the first day or two that it takes for  this review to go through you are not  going to be making money so your  subscribers are gonna be watching your  video but you're not gonna be making  money off that video until they approve  the review and that could be two days  later when most of the views on that  video have already been gotten so you're  not making that money back imagine that  you earn a hundred dollars a day at your  9 to 5 job you go in one day you earn a  hundred dollars you go in the next day  you do the same amount of work by your  employer tells you sorry your work was  deemed unsuitable for all customers so  I'm only going to pay you 10 percent of  what I paid you yesterday now you don't  know what they're talking about because  there's nothing wrong with your work so  you request a review and two days later  they get back to you and say yeah  actually you were right there was  nothing wrong with your work however  we're not gonna give you the money that  you would have gotten because it's too  late now those customers that were here  are now gone your viewers on YouTube  that saw the video without ads are gone  so you will not be making that money  back even though you did nothing wrong  and there was nothing wrong with your  video  it was our mistake so yeah this is  definitely a really difficult situation  for any youtuber trying to make them  living on YouTube because especially if  you have a lot of subscribers like a  million subscribers like the anime man  Aki dearest lost pause misty connects  yeah and you upload a video and all your  subscribers get the notification and  watching the first day or two if this  video is flagged even if it was  wrongfully flagged and eventually upon  review they approve it you will not be  making money from your own subscribers  watching your videos so definitely a  really difficult situation we'll see how  it goes maybe YouTube will actually fix  this system I don't know but I will keep  you posted in case there's any sort of  community effort to fight against this  to stand up to this and another non  YouTube new